WEBVTT

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:03.169
- Previously on The O.C.:
- I can't do this anymore. I don't trust you.

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:04.754
Oliver's not stable. He's dangerous.

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:07.631
Oliver has not done anything to Marissa
except be her friend.

00:00:07.798 --> 00:00:10.217
Look, you guys may not believe me.
No one may believe me.

00:00:10.384 --> 00:00:11.551
- Theresa.
- Ryan Atwood.

00:00:11.718 --> 00:00:13.803
- So you two were...
- We grew up together.

00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:16.389
I always had a crush on you.

00:00:17.431 --> 00:00:18.474
You should go.

00:00:18.641 --> 00:00:21.226
I'm not gonna stand here and pretend
like I'm your girlfriend when I'm not.

00:00:21.435 --> 00:00:22.477
At least not anymore.

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:24.812
Put the gun down,
you get a second chance.

00:00:25.021 --> 00:00:29.233
- I'm sorry. You were right.
- It's okay. It's okay.

00:00:42.577 --> 00:00:45.872
Happy Valentine's Day.
Someone just got struck by cupid's arrow.

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.624
Happy Valentine's Day.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:53.044
- Valentine's Day's not till tomorrow.
- You're not excited?

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:57.506
I am. I am. I'm just still thinking
about Oliver with that gun.

00:00:57.715 --> 00:00:59.716
- I know.
- Who knows what could've happened?

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:02.510
But it didn't.
And Dr. Kim lifted Ryan's suspension.

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:05.555
So the best thing is for
everything to return to normal.

00:01:05.763 --> 00:01:08.891
And in this house that means
celebrating the holidays.

00:01:09.099 --> 00:01:12.227
Valentine's Day is not a holiday.
Rosh Hashanah, that's a holiday.

00:01:12.394 --> 00:01:16.063
Memorial Day? Yes, a holiday.
You know who invented Valentine's Day?

00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:18.232
- St. Valentine.
- Hershey's and Hallmark.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.067
If you're single, it depresses you.

00:01:20.275 --> 00:01:22.986
If you are in love, start shelling out.
Chocolate. Flowers.

00:01:23.153 --> 00:01:24.987
- Lingerie.
- You never bought me lingerie.

00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:27.198
See how upset you are?
I hate this holiday.

00:01:27.406 --> 00:01:30.075
- Must be talking about Valentine's Day.
- I am. I hate it.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:36.247
- Hey. You got me.
- Guess who got shot by cupid's arrow.

00:01:36.455 --> 00:01:37.706
Is someone going overboard?

00:01:37.915 --> 00:01:39.875
You're one to talk.
Chrismukkah, anyone?

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:42.752
- At least that's a real holiday.
- Tell her, Dad. It's two.

00:01:42.961 --> 00:01:45.505
- Seth made that word up when he was 6.
- It's an important...

00:01:45.713 --> 00:01:48.132
This is an important holiday.
It's Valentine's Day.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.259
- Where Jewishness fuses with Christianity.
- Do the math.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.059
- How you doing, kid?
- You know. Okay, I guess.

00:02:01.268 --> 00:02:05.813
You're about to be great. Tomorrow
is the big Valentine's Day Singles' Gala.

00:02:06.022 --> 00:02:08.274
A benefit for Newport Memorial's
Heart Department.

00:02:08.482 --> 00:02:11.943
Big party. You guys are gonna dress up.
Everyone's gonna be there.

00:02:12.152 --> 00:02:15.696
Just like normal, huh? Yes!

00:02:21.284 --> 00:02:22.285
I'm gonna go.

00:03:05.488 --> 00:03:08.324
- Ryan. Hey.
- Hey.

00:03:14.495 --> 00:03:15.955
Were you able to sleep at all?

00:03:16.122 --> 00:03:17.498
- Not much.
- Me either.

00:03:17.665 --> 00:03:20.334
- I kept going over everything in my head.
- Yeah.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.336
He's in the hospital,
so hopefully he'll get better.

00:03:23.545 --> 00:03:25.004
I hope so.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:29.258
I'm ready for everything to just
go back to normal. The way it was.

00:03:32.302 --> 00:03:35.596
Great. So, Valentine's Day tomorrow.

00:03:35.805 --> 00:03:37.973
- Yeah?
- What were you gonna do? Because...

00:03:38.182 --> 00:03:40.267
...I didn't know if you wanted to...
- Yeah, no.

00:03:40.475 --> 00:03:43.144
- Kirsten's hosting this singles' dance...
- For the hospital.

00:03:43.353 --> 00:03:45.480
I told her I'd go.
I didn't know if you wanted...

00:03:45.688 --> 00:03:46.981
Of course.

00:03:48.148 --> 00:03:50.984
Right. Well, then I'll go too.

00:03:52.611 --> 00:03:54.946
Who knows?
Maybe we'll meet somebody there.

00:03:55.154 --> 00:03:56.614
Yeah. Who knows?

00:04:00.784 --> 00:04:05.580
- All right. I should get to...
- Yeah. No. Me too.

00:04:25.763 --> 00:04:26.931
Hey, Summer.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:28.849
God, Cohen. You made me mess up.

00:04:29.058 --> 00:04:32.143
- I'm going for the high score.
- Hey, it's good to see you too.

00:04:32.352 --> 00:04:35.104
- Tomorrow's Valentine's Day.
- Oh, really?

00:04:35.271 --> 00:04:37.731
God. I didn't know tomorrow
was Valentine's Day.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.942
But thanks for reminding me.
Have fun with Anna.

00:04:41.151 --> 00:04:43.820
- Anna's in Pittsburgh for the weekend.
- On Valentine's Day?

00:04:44.028 --> 00:04:45.655
Hey, now that's commitment.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.616
Actually, Anna and I broke up.

00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:52.118
And I wanted to see
what you're doing tomorrow.

00:04:56.497 --> 00:04:58.499
- So you guys broke up.
- Yeah.

00:04:58.707 --> 00:05:02.752
Coffee. You're single now and you want
to know what I'm doing for Valentine's.

00:05:02.961 --> 00:05:04.587
- Yeah.
- So Anna dumps you...

00:05:04.754 --> 00:05:08.090
...and you think you can choose me
and I'd still be interested in you?

00:05:08.299 --> 00:05:11.510
First of all, what makes you think
that Anna dumped me?

00:05:11.718 --> 00:05:13.845
Never mind. Second of all...

00:05:14.387 --> 00:05:17.807
...kind of. Yes.
- Yeah. No. No way.

00:05:18.015 --> 00:05:20.225
I'm not gonna be your
sloppy seconds, ass-face.

00:05:20.559 --> 00:05:23.228
Besides, I'm busy tomorrow.
I'll be at the singles' dance.

00:05:23.436 --> 00:05:24.979
- So will I.
- I don't care.

00:05:25.188 --> 00:05:26.355
- See you there.
- Not if I see you first.

00:05:26.564 --> 00:05:30.359
- Maybe we'll both meet someone special.
- Yeah, as long as his name isn't Cohen.

00:05:32.277 --> 00:05:33.987
Snap.

00:05:36.364 --> 00:05:37.490
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:05:37.698 --> 00:05:40.701
Crusading for the rich and dysfunctional
is time-consuming.

00:05:40.867 --> 00:05:42.911
Let me just dot my I's and cross my T's.

00:05:43.119 --> 00:05:46.664
Come on, I'm starving. I've been thinking
about crab cakes for the last hour.

00:05:46.872 --> 00:05:48.832
Will you be around tomorrow
to help set up?

00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:51.960
- For what?
- The Valentine's Day Single Dance Gala.

00:05:52.168 --> 00:05:55.338
No. I can't do it.
I got this petty nuisance lawsuit. In fact...

00:05:56.005 --> 00:05:57.965
...I'm pretty booked this weekend.

00:05:58.173 --> 00:06:02.636
So I might be a little late to
the Valentine's Day Dance Singles' Gala.

00:06:02.844 --> 00:06:04.595
- Singles.
- Singles' Dance Gala.

00:06:05.179 --> 00:06:06.347
Why?

00:06:06.555 --> 00:06:08.932
- We said we'd go together.
- It's restaurant stuff.

00:06:09.141 --> 00:06:12.143
Got the zoning inspectors coming by
before we can expand the deck.

00:06:12.352 --> 00:06:14.979
- On Saturday?
- I guess these city council guys are busy.

00:06:15.188 --> 00:06:17.481
- No. I forbid it.
- You what?

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.067
With whatever wifely authority
I have vested in me...

00:06:20.275 --> 00:06:22.777
...on this most holy
and romantic of days, no.

00:06:22.986 --> 00:06:27.573
- It's only a holiday. Not even a real one.
- Not this again. Not on an empty stomach.

00:06:27.781 --> 00:06:31.368
How about Arbor Day? Trees?
That's a good cause. Or Secretary's Day.

00:06:31.576 --> 00:06:34.412
- How about our anniversary?
- Which we might not make it to.

00:06:34.621 --> 00:06:36.747
You know you'll have more fun
without me.

00:06:36.956 --> 00:06:40.083
No. You're going.
Sandy, this is important to me.

00:06:40.292 --> 00:06:42.794
There's a lot of things
important to me that you don't do.

00:06:43.003 --> 00:06:44.212
- Like what?
- Like golfing.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.339
- Lots of couples golf together.
- Shortly before dying of old age.

00:06:47.548 --> 00:06:50.092
Surfing. How often have I tried
to get you in the ocean?

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.428
- With the fish?
- And still I'm patient. I'm forgiving.

00:06:53.678 --> 00:06:55.721
- You're joking.
- I put up with your father.

00:06:55.972 --> 00:06:59.349
- You're eligible for sainthood any day.
- I forgive your snoring.

00:06:59.558 --> 00:07:02.102
- I do not snore.
- Yeah, you do.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.437
Like a freight train
roaring through the house.

00:07:04.646 --> 00:07:06.731
You wanted to do this restaurant,
I supported you.

00:07:06.939 --> 00:07:10.567
You wanted to go into private practice,
who had your back?

00:07:10.776 --> 00:07:14.195
- I put up with your father.
- You never wanna do anything I like.

00:07:14.404 --> 00:07:16.072
Everything's a fight, an argument.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.408
- My life, my job.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, and I'm still here.

00:07:19.616 --> 00:07:21.410
- Don't do me any favors.
- I won't.

00:07:21.618 --> 00:07:23.078
- Fine.
- Perfect.

00:07:23.953 --> 00:07:25.872
- What are we fighting about?
- I'm not sure.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.456
But it's serious.

00:07:27.832 --> 00:07:30.292
You're on your own for lunch.

00:07:31.418 --> 00:07:33.128
Happy Valentine's Day.

00:07:38.173 --> 00:07:40.384
Hey, kiddo.

00:07:40.884 --> 00:07:44.012
Plasterer came to the restaurant today.
Made a total mess.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.222
But progress is being made.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:48.766
- How's school?
- Okay.

00:07:48.974 --> 00:07:50.851
- Yeah?
- Hey, you got something.

00:07:51.059 --> 00:07:53.269
It was left for you at the door.

00:07:55.063 --> 00:07:59.274
Well, it's not ticking,
so it can't be from your mom.

00:08:00.192 --> 00:08:02.444
"Hope you're not too Ionely
this Valentine's Day.

00:08:02.652 --> 00:08:05.571
X O, X O. Your Secret Admirer."

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.782
Marissa, you're so sweet.
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:08.949 --> 00:08:11.118
- I didn't.
- Well...

00:08:11.326 --> 00:08:14.078
...who else would've left something nice?
- Good question.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.665
This year I'm doing my best
to avoid Valentine's Day completely.

00:08:18.165 --> 00:08:22.335
- What? You and Ryan are...?
- I don't really want to talk about it.

00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:26.839
- And neither does he.
- Well, it is Valentine's Day.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:32.093
Sometimes the big romantic gesture
is more effective than talking.

00:08:33.887 --> 00:08:36.472
There's no way your mom
gave me these, right? No.

00:08:36.681 --> 00:08:39.975
She doesn't make her disdain for me
a secret. Much less her admiration.

00:08:40.183 --> 00:08:42.060
Well, have you kissed anyone recently?

00:08:43.394 --> 00:08:45.188
Previously on The Valley:

00:08:45.354 --> 00:08:47.857
I just don 't feel like I fit
here in Tarzana.

00:08:48.065 --> 00:08:49.775
I'm busy. Studying...

00:08:49.983 --> 00:08:51.776
...naked.

00:08:51.943 --> 00:08:54.612
Is that supposed to keep me away?

00:08:55.196 --> 00:08:56.906
Cohen?

00:08:59.992 --> 00:09:02.035
- You're at my house.
- And you're dressed.

00:09:02.244 --> 00:09:04.579
I wonder who's more disappointed.

00:09:05.079 --> 00:09:06.080
- Can I come in?
- No.

00:09:06.289 --> 00:09:07.331
Thanks.

00:09:08.332 --> 00:09:10.334
What are you doing here?

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.378
Who's this?

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:14.962
- No one.
- "I'm not no one."

00:09:15.129 --> 00:09:17.673
- Princess Sparkle. What do you want?
- She's Captain Oats' type.

00:09:17.882 --> 00:09:20.259
You tell him to keep his hooves off.
As for you...

00:09:20.467 --> 00:09:24.595
Wait, wait. Before you kick me out, can
you please give me a second to explain?

00:09:26.138 --> 00:09:28.432
Okay, listen. Summer...

00:09:30.225 --> 00:09:32.519
...it's not like...

00:09:32.727 --> 00:09:35.980
...now that me and Anna broke up
I'm now choosing you.

00:09:36.188 --> 00:09:37.815
Okay?

00:09:39.358 --> 00:09:42.861
Because the whole reason
that we broke up...

00:09:43.069 --> 00:09:45.154
...is because for me...

00:09:47.615 --> 00:09:50.117
...it's always been you, Summer.

00:09:50.325 --> 00:09:52.118
It's always been you.

00:09:52.327 --> 00:09:54.871
I've tried to fight it,
and I've tried to deny it.

00:09:55.079 --> 00:09:57.832
And I can't. I can't do it.

00:09:57.998 --> 00:09:59.958
You're undeniable.

00:10:16.514 --> 00:10:18.599
- Cohen?
- Yeah.

00:10:18.807 --> 00:10:20.559
Do you happen...

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.394
...to have...

00:10:23.603 --> 00:10:25.563
...you know...?
- Oh...

00:10:26.689 --> 00:10:29.358
...yeah, I do. In my wallet.
- Yeah?

00:10:29.566 --> 00:10:33.778
I was beginning to view it as sort of
a rabbit's foot, for good luck only, but...

00:10:33.987 --> 00:10:36.280
You're about to get lucky.

00:10:43.411 --> 00:10:45.872
Whatever you say, Summer. Yes.

00:10:46.247 --> 00:10:47.957
Yes.

00:11:03.636 --> 00:11:05.972
- Luke. Hi.
- Hi, Mrs. Cooper.

00:11:06.764 --> 00:11:08.599
What are you doing here?

00:11:12.102 --> 00:11:15.813
Do you know...? I was wondering,
did Marissa bring her bio textbook home?

00:11:16.022 --> 00:11:19.274
Marissa doesn't live here anymore, Luke.
You know that.

00:11:19.525 --> 00:11:22.027
Right. I must have forgot.

00:11:24.612 --> 00:11:27.073
Right. Okay. Well, good night.

00:11:27.781 --> 00:11:32.369
Tomorrow is the Valentine's Day party.
Are you gonna go?

00:11:32.577 --> 00:11:36.497
Because I'm gonna go.
And I thought if you needed a ride...

00:11:37.289 --> 00:11:39.833
Actually, everything that's happened
with Caleb and me...

00:11:40.042 --> 00:11:42.419
...I think it's best I stay home.
Avoid this holiday.

00:11:42.627 --> 00:11:43.920
Yeah.

00:11:44.128 --> 00:11:46.422
It's just another day of the week, right?

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.509
Okay.

00:11:50.717 --> 00:11:53.887
- Good night, Mrs. Cooper.
- Good night.

00:12:06.814 --> 00:12:08.357
So...

00:12:08.524 --> 00:12:10.359
...that was sex.

00:12:10.901 --> 00:12:12.527
Yep.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.739
- I'm gonna go.
- Me too.

00:12:16.947 --> 00:12:18.407
But you live here.

00:12:18.574 --> 00:12:20.534
I meant downstairs.

00:12:20.742 --> 00:12:22.118
Okay.

00:12:22.285 --> 00:12:23.912
Perfect.

00:12:45.304 --> 00:12:46.764
Hi.

00:12:55.229 --> 00:12:57.523
I love you so much.

00:13:00.108 --> 00:13:02.694
We've waited a long time to...

00:13:02.902 --> 00:13:08.365
...you know, and I thought maybe
we could start Valentine's Day early.

00:13:11.827 --> 00:13:14.495
- No. Wait. Wait. Hold on.
- What?

00:13:14.662 --> 00:13:16.414
Don't you want to?

00:13:16.622 --> 00:13:18.082
No.

00:13:20.125 --> 00:13:21.835
No. I mean, yeah.

00:13:22.002 --> 00:13:23.545
Yeah, of course.

00:13:24.337 --> 00:13:27.006
But with everything that's happened,
it just...

00:13:27.173 --> 00:13:30.509
- It seems a little soon.
- I just wish it hadn't happened.

00:13:30.717 --> 00:13:33.470
That we could still be like we were...

00:13:35.096 --> 00:13:38.349
...and I wanted to make it up to you.
- You don't have to...

00:13:38.557 --> 00:13:40.475
...do this.

00:13:41.393 --> 00:13:43.228
No. You're right.

00:13:43.436 --> 00:13:46.897
So I guess I'll go.

00:13:47.106 --> 00:13:49.191
- Because this is just really...
- Wrong?

00:13:50.234 --> 00:13:53.111
I was gonna say "embarrassing."
But I guess "wrong" works.

00:13:53.319 --> 00:13:58.866
So it was nice to see you.
And I guess I'll see you again tomorrow.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:15.922
- Hey, buddy. Got some big news.
- I was about to go set up. You coming?

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.965
It's a lot of lifting. It's not my thing.

00:14:18.173 --> 00:14:21.176
I don't know if I just mentioned this,
but I have some big news.

00:14:21.384 --> 00:14:24.470
- Yeah, so I heard. What's up?
- Ryan, I'm a man now.

00:14:24.679 --> 00:14:27.807
Not just like an after-your-bar-mitzvah
man, but a "man" man.

00:14:28.015 --> 00:14:31.893
I had sex with a girl.
Summer, to be more specific.

00:14:32.102 --> 00:14:33.978
How was it?

00:14:34.646 --> 00:14:36.230
- I had sex.
- That bad?

00:14:36.856 --> 00:14:39.858
No, not that bad...

00:14:40.067 --> 00:14:42.110
...just kind of weird.
- Weird?

00:14:42.319 --> 00:14:45.947
Yeah, but not kinky weird.
More like weird awkward.

00:14:46.155 --> 00:14:49.116
But, hey, it was my first time.
She's a more experienced woman.

00:14:49.324 --> 00:14:50.492
That's to be expected.

00:14:50.701 --> 00:14:55.496
And I did make some faces in the middle
that I wish I could take back, but I can't.

00:14:55.705 --> 00:14:59.249
There was also sort of a whiny noise
that came out towards the end...

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.378
...that probably wasn't my finest hour.
I sucked so bad.

00:15:03.586 --> 00:15:06.422
I was like a fish flopping around
on dry land.

00:15:06.631 --> 00:15:10.676
Ryan, I was Nemo.
And I just wanted to go home.

00:15:10.926 --> 00:15:14.804
- Don't worry. You'll get another chance.
- That's the thing. I'm not sure I will.

00:15:15.013 --> 00:15:19.433
The situation with Summer is murkier now
than it was before the awful fish sex.

00:15:19.641 --> 00:15:21.226
I wouldn't refer to it as fish sex.

00:15:21.435 --> 00:15:24.395
Good point. That's something
I was hoping to get more of: Tips.

00:15:24.604 --> 00:15:28.023
Tricks of the trade. Summer's used to
driving a higher performance vehicle.

00:15:28.232 --> 00:15:30.484
Don't know if I'm the guy
to talk to about romance.

00:15:30.692 --> 00:15:31.902
- Why?
- Me and Marissa.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:35.113
- It's different now, post-Oliver.
- Yeah? You wanna talk about it?

00:15:35.321 --> 00:15:37.740
- No, I should get over to set up.
- Hey.

00:15:37.948 --> 00:15:40.075
So do you have tips
or words of wisdom for me?

00:15:40.284 --> 00:15:41.827
Do it again.

00:15:43.078 --> 00:15:45.371
That's what I was afraid of.

00:15:47.623 --> 00:15:52.377
And then we both just decided to wait.
Because, you know, we were really tired.

00:15:52.585 --> 00:15:54.504
Well, you know how it goes.

00:15:57.423 --> 00:16:00.342
- I wish we had waited.
- What? Who?

00:16:00.926 --> 00:16:02.844
Me and Cohen.

00:16:03.178 --> 00:16:05.263
- We had sex.
- Wait, what?

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.223
