00:32:58.732 --> 00:33:01.943
Valentine's Day is wonderful, isn't it?

00:33:03.570 --> 00:33:08.032
- You know, the thing about Ryan...
- No, this isn't...

00:33:08.407 --> 00:33:10.450
- It's not... I'm fine.
- I know.

00:33:10.659 --> 00:33:14.871
But the thing about Ryan is,
whenever things have gotten tough...

00:33:15.079 --> 00:33:18.165
...everyone in his life has abandoned him.
- That's what he thinks I did.

00:33:18.374 --> 00:33:19.833
Surprise him. Show him you didn't.

00:33:20.167 --> 00:33:22.669
- That you're not gonna give up on him.
- He wants me to.

00:33:22.877 --> 00:33:26.297
Well, only because he expects you to.
It's crazy.

00:33:26.672 --> 00:33:27.882
Love is crazy.

00:33:28.090 --> 00:33:30.842
It's always challenging. It's never easy.

00:33:31.009 --> 00:33:33.887
- Yeah, but is it always this hard?
- Sometimes.

00:33:34.095 --> 00:33:36.138
But you hang in there anyway.

00:33:36.347 --> 00:33:38.599
If you're having the worst fight
in the world...

00:33:38.807 --> 00:33:42.727
...or some stupid argument that neither
of you can remember what it's about.

00:33:42.936 --> 00:33:44.646
Because it's...

00:33:44.854 --> 00:33:46.647
It's worth it.

00:33:48.732 --> 00:33:50.901
You guys have been
through so much already.

00:33:51.359 --> 00:33:53.319
Why quit now?

00:33:56.364 --> 00:33:58.032
- Hey, Mr. Cohen.
- Hello, Summer.

00:33:58.240 --> 00:34:01.034
- Hi. Coop, you ready to go?
- Yeah.

00:34:01.243 --> 00:34:03.620
- You okay, kiddo?
- Yeah. Thanks.

00:34:12.377 --> 00:34:15.838
- Sometimes you make it hard to hate you.
- I know.

00:34:16.047 --> 00:34:19.133
It's all... It's all... It's part of my charm.

00:34:19.341 --> 00:34:21.718
Sometimes you make it easy.

00:34:23.720 --> 00:34:27.389
- Charming too, no?
- Let's go home.

00:34:49.366 --> 00:34:51.868
You tried to jump that fence
and your pants got caught.

00:34:52.077 --> 00:34:53.244
I was pretty graceful.

00:34:53.453 --> 00:34:56.789
- Yeah, especially when you face-planted.
- Glad to see you enjoy my pain.

00:34:56.997 --> 00:34:59.833
We had no ice and we had to use
that bag of frozen peas.

00:35:00.042 --> 00:35:03.336
Yeah. Frozen vegetables.
The miracle cure.

00:35:05.838 --> 00:35:09.466
It's pretty amazing, us running into
each other on Valentine's Day.

00:35:12.927 --> 00:35:15.680
I gotta get back. Help clean up.

00:35:17.139 --> 00:35:20.058
So do you go to a lot
of these kinds of events?

00:35:21.101 --> 00:35:23.186
Pretty much every week.

00:35:23.728 --> 00:35:26.480
Well, then maybe I'll run into you again.

00:35:27.398 --> 00:35:29.983
Plus, I know where you live.

00:35:35.780 --> 00:35:38.532
- Oh, God.
- I know I shouldn't be here.

00:35:38.866 --> 00:35:41.368
- No, you shouldn't, Luke.
- But it's just...

00:35:41.576 --> 00:35:43.578
I don't know,
you looked so sad when you left.

00:35:43.786 --> 00:35:47.206
I couldn't bear the thought of you
being alone on Valentine's Day.

00:35:47.415 --> 00:35:50.000
Most people would enjoy that thought.

00:35:50.209 --> 00:35:51.793
Not me.

00:35:52.711 --> 00:35:56.214
Mrs. Cooper, you are an amazing girl.

00:35:57.798 --> 00:35:59.258
Woman.

00:35:59.800 --> 00:36:01.343
Lady.

00:36:01.760 --> 00:36:05.096
- Lf Mr. Nichol doesn't appreciate you...
- No. He sure doesn't.

00:36:05.304 --> 00:36:09.266
That's because he's too old to see
what he's lucky enough to have.

00:36:12.269 --> 00:36:16.397
And you should also know that
you have always been the coolest mom.

00:36:16.647 --> 00:36:18.816
- Luke.
- It's true. You let us listen to...

00:36:19.024 --> 00:36:23.570
...whatever we wanted to in the carpool.
And you let us watch R-rated movies.

00:36:23.778 --> 00:36:28.532
- And whenever we played Ultimatum...
- Ultimatum?

00:36:29.867 --> 00:36:34.704
You know, who, of all your
friends' moms, would you rather do?

00:36:35.830 --> 00:36:38.832
- That's a game?
- And whenever we played it...

00:36:39.041 --> 00:36:42.252
...you always won.
- Really?

00:36:42.877 --> 00:36:45.796
- I beat Kirsten?
- I thought you should know the truth...

00:36:46.005 --> 00:36:48.048
...on Valentine's Day.

00:36:50.676 --> 00:36:52.344
- Good night.
- Wait.

00:37:05.605 --> 00:37:06.856
Thank you.

00:37:32.294 --> 00:37:34.254
Would you like to come in?

00:37:43.136 --> 00:37:46.264
I guess you're happy that today is over.

00:37:46.472 --> 00:37:48.349
Absolutely.

00:37:57.106 --> 00:37:59.775
Oh, my God, Sandy.

00:38:00.108 --> 00:38:03.570
Somebody's got to keep
Hershey's and Hallmark in business.

00:38:11.535 --> 00:38:14.370
- So you want to be my Valentine?
- Yes.

00:38:14.537 --> 00:38:19.041
Just as soon as I have some of these
caramel chocolates. They're my favorite.

00:38:19.249 --> 00:38:22.002
The square ones.
I like the ones with nuts.

00:38:23.920 --> 00:38:27.840
Not to rub it in, man,
but I think Princess Sparkle is your type.

00:38:28.132 --> 00:38:30.384
Yeah, I blew it for us both.

00:38:30.759 --> 00:38:31.927
What's that?

00:38:32.135 --> 00:38:34.012
Yeah. Are you kidding?
Great hooves.

00:38:35.471 --> 00:38:38.140
- Cohen?
- Summer.

00:38:38.307 --> 00:38:40.183
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:38:43.311 --> 00:38:44.771
No.

00:38:47.940 --> 00:38:49.650
The other night...

00:38:50.442 --> 00:38:51.985
...when we...

00:38:52.527 --> 00:38:55.363
...had sex.
- Yeah.

00:38:57.031 --> 00:38:59.283
You weren't the only virgin in the room.

00:38:59.950 --> 00:39:02.327
There was someone else in the room?
Like, filming us?

00:39:02.535 --> 00:39:04.454
Me, jackass.

00:39:04.829 --> 00:39:07.206
I'm a virgin.

00:39:07.415 --> 00:39:09.875
Or I was a virgin.

00:39:12.627 --> 00:39:14.545
Why didn't you tell me?

00:39:14.754 --> 00:39:16.797
I don't know.

00:39:17.089 --> 00:39:21.843
I guess I felt like
I had this reputation to uphold...

00:39:22.385 --> 00:39:25.555
...and I figured you'd think less of me.
- No.

00:39:25.888 --> 00:39:29.683
Are you kidding? Not at all.
I'm just... I'm shocked.

00:39:30.309 --> 00:39:35.021
God. Never in a million years would I
think that you, of all people, not that...

00:39:35.229 --> 00:39:37.648
That is not what's important here.

00:39:38.982 --> 00:39:41.818
This was a huge moment in our lives
and we just blew past it.

00:39:42.027 --> 00:39:44.028
- Really quickly.
- Hey, not that quickly.

00:39:45.488 --> 00:39:47.490
Pretty quickly, yes.

00:39:48.741 --> 00:39:50.492
And it was a big deal.

00:39:50.701 --> 00:39:53.912
I think that it should've been special.

00:39:54.120 --> 00:39:56.038
And we rushed it.

00:39:58.540 --> 00:40:00.626
What if...

00:40:01.209 --> 00:40:03.670
...we were to slow it down a little bit?

00:40:04.337 --> 00:40:06.339
Maybe...

00:40:06.756 --> 00:40:08.841
...start from the beginning?

00:40:09.383 --> 00:40:11.009
What do you mean?

00:40:25.021 --> 00:40:28.816
- You are so cheesy, Cohen.
- Come on.

00:40:29.024 --> 00:40:31.276
I'm sweeping you off your feet.

00:40:32.819 --> 00:40:36.364
Well, the sad part is...

00:40:37.406 --> 00:40:39.324
...you kind of are.

00:41:11.893 --> 00:41:13.853
- Where is she?
- What?

00:41:14.062 --> 00:41:17.857
Theresa. If she's here, I want her
to know I'm not gonna lose you.

00:41:18.065 --> 00:41:20.192
I'm not gonna give up on you.

00:41:20.400 --> 00:41:22.235
She left.

00:41:23.445 --> 00:41:26.614
- I'm so sorry.
- I know.

00:41:35.246 --> 00:41:37.498
Can't you just forgive me?

00:41:38.666 --> 00:41:40.083
How?

00:41:43.294 --> 00:41:45.213
I don't know...

00:41:46.214 --> 00:41:48.299
...if we should be together.

00:41:49.383 --> 00:41:54.721
I mean, look how easy it was for someone
to come into our lives, come between us.

00:41:57.056 --> 00:41:59.975
- How do I know it won't happen again?
- It won't.

00:42:00.142 --> 00:42:02.686
- You have to trust me.
- Like you trusted me.

00:42:04.479 --> 00:42:06.105
Ryan.

00:42:09.900 --> 00:42:11.359
So that's it?

00:42:14.195 --> 00:42:16.739
I can't pretend it didn't happen.
